   {
    "id": "GB2481116",
    "source": "PAT",
    "title": "Apparatus for helping a baby to sleep",
    "authorString": "BRADSHAW LUCY JANE.",
    "authorList": {
     "author": [
      {
       "fullName": "BRADSHAW LUCY JANE",
       "lastName": "BRADSHAW LUCY JANE"
      }
     ]
    },
    "pubYear": "2011",
    "abstractText": "An apparatus 2 is provided for assisting a baby to sleep. The apparatus comprises a sound unit 4 arranged to provide soothing sounds to the baby, and a band 6 being worn on the wrist or ankle of the baby. The apparatus is arranged such that the band is in wireless communication with the sound unit. The band includes a motion detector for detecting movement of the baby whereby the band causes the sound unit to produce soothing sounds upon detecting movement of the baby. The band device further causes the sound unit to cease producing the soothing sounds upon the motion detector no longer detecting movement of the baby. The apparatus may operate in a cyclical manner firstly providing soothing sounds when the baby is awake in order to get the baby to fall asleep, and secondly providing soothing sounds after the baby emerges from a sleep stage. The soothing sounds may be womb sound. The motion detector may comprise an accelerometer.",
    "affiliation": "BRADSHAW LUCY JANE",
    "language": "eng",
